To your comments/exemplar issues, that seems to me to fit with exactly what I'm saying above, you have separate issues (ostensibly derived from conversations here and in other places).  They appear to have concrete problem statements, and suggestions for action that can be debated, and decided upon.  The remaining piece that is unclear is what constitutes 'done' for this issue.  With such an identifier as described above, we could effectively say "This issue is never 'done'" from a planning standpoint, so that any scheduling concerns are moot.  The only thing that remains then is the can we kick down the road if we wind up with 1000's if stale investegatory issues, but thats a bridge we can cross when we come to it.
